            "text": "If I could change the world in one way, I\u2019d hard-wire empathy into how we see and treat one another. Imagine growing up in a world where, from an early age, every child learns not just to read and write but to truly listen, to recognize others\u2019 joys and fears as their own. \n\nWith empathy as our guiding principle:\n\n\u2022 Conflicts would be approached as shared problems rather than zero-sum contests.  \n\u2022 Inequalities\u2014whether of income, opportunity or basic rights\u2014would feel unacceptable, because we\u2019d genuinely feel our neighbors\u2019 struggles.  \n\u2022 Cooperation on global crises like climate change or pandemics would come naturally, driven by a sense of \u201cwe\u2019re in this together,\u201d not narrow self-interest.  \n\u2022 Advances in science, technology and policy would be measured not just by profit or power but by the real human flourishing they produce.\n\nIn short, if each of us could instinctively step into another person\u2019s shoes\u2014across cultures, across languages, across borders\u2014we\u2019d transform fear and division into understanding and shared responsibility. That one shift in perspective could reshape every institution and every relationship on the planet."
